  "notes": "Opt-in map from all 66 Mesh2Motion (M2M) source joints to the frozen 50-bone 'polygon_humanoid' rig in the Godot project. The pinned M2M skeleton.glb has 66 joints including root, clavicle_*, ball_* and *_leaf joints; the 58-name HumanChainConfig list is a subset. Map keys are the M2M names expected in the exported GLB; values are Godot Skeleton3D bone names. DROP means the source chain has no target (head_leaf, thumb_04_leaf, ring_* and pinky_* chains) and is discarded; the three face helpers are synthesized at rest. 47 mapped targets + 3 synthesized = the frozen 50-bone rig. Rig conventions: 1 unit = 1 m, Y up, -Z forward, feet at y=0, armature node 'Armature' with a 'Skeleton3D' child, animation track paths 'Armature/Skeleton3D:<bone>', root motion stripped so Root translation stays constant. Used by src.validate --profile and by the optional Godot-side bone rename."
